From: PanVK G615 Migration <panvk-migration@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENTAL: refresh 002-android-release-queue-mesa27.patch against the G615-only dependency series

Purpose: EXPERIMENTAL: refresh 002-android-release-queue-mesa27.patch against the G615-only dependency series
Source/Reference: Mesa 13baeb70c066a9f82d2bcfb29f06e4865212affa and the retired JM patch inventory.
Tested GPU: not run for this extracted series (target: Mali-G615).
Tested Kbase UAPI: not run for this extracted series (target: CSF 1.21).
Mesa base range: 27.0.0-devel (13baeb70c066a9f82d2bcfb29f06e4865212affa).
Dependencies: preceding G615 profile patches in scripts/apply-patches.sh.
Validation test: G615 host regressions, strict replay, Android and glibc builds.

Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] panvk: Android release and cross-queue GPU waits on Kbase

Mesa base: 13baeb70c066a9f82d2bcfb29f06e4865212affa plus the G615 profile.
Requires Android 018 (historical 0178) for native-buffer import.
Includes the original Android release callback fix; replaces revision 1 of 002.
The GPU-wait update uses producer seqno addresses for cross-queue dependencies,
rejects external sync-file/non-CSF payloads in peek, skips already-retired
seqnos, and stages per-subqueue wait updates transactionally.

